# Dual-issue Step 4a demo: a memory op in LANE 0 paired with an ALU in lane 1.
# Two aligned pairs, run in a loop so they are fetched warm (issue_two):
#   {2,3}: lane 0 = ST [r1], r2   (memory)   ; lane 1 = ADD r3, r2, r2   (ALU)
#   {4,5}: lane 0 = LD r4, [r1]   (memory)   ; lane 1 = ADD r5, r3, r3   (ALU)
# Lane 1 is a simple ALU in both (no memory, no branch), and neither lane 1 reads
# lane 0's load destination (no unbypassable load-use), so both pairs issue
# together: the pc jumps 2 -> 4 -> 6 every iteration. r4 loads back the stored 7,
# proving a store then a load through the cache inside dual bundles.
6440   # 0: LI   r1, 64         (base data address)
6807   # 1: LI   r2, 7          (value to store)
a0a0   # 2: ST   [r1], r2       (lane 0 memory; mem[64] = 7)
2d20   # 3: ADD  r3, r2, r2     (lane 1 ALU; r3 = 14)
9080   # 4: LD   r4, [r1]       (lane 0 memory; r4 = mem[64] = 7)
35b0   # 5: ADD  r5, r3, r3     (lane 1 ALU; r5 = 28)
c002   # 6: BEQZ r0, 2          (r0 = 0 -> taken; loop back to the pairs)
0000   # 7: NOP
